meta {
  name: security
  seq: 16
}

tests {
  test("an operator never logs anyone in or matches a record", () => {
    expect(res.status).to.be.within(400, 404)
    expect(res.body).to.not.have.property("token")
  })
}

docs {
  NoSQL operator injection: each request sends an operator object (like { "$ne": null }) where the API expects a plain value, and must get 400, 401 or 404 with no token in the answer. Nothing is saved: every request fails before a write.
  Two layers are tested together: the type checks in the controllers, and mongoose.set("sanitizeFilter", true) behind them.

  Self-contained: request 1 logs in the admin and the waiter, picks a category and computes openDate, then sends its own check. Run the folder in order.

  Login limit: failed logins count, 10 per IP every 15 minutes. This folder sends 2 (requests 1 and 2), the auth folder 2. Before a second full run within 15 minutes, restart the backend (type rs in the nodemon terminal): the count lives in memory.
  On render (liveCaptcha = true) the booking requests with a valid party size are refused by Turnstile first: they expect 400 CAPTCHA_FAILED instead of their own code.
}
